### Resolve the project root first

Before any `git`, `gh`, or `{{ issueflows_dir }}/` operation, settle `<project_root>` and `<owner/repo>`, stopping at the first unambiguous answer: explicit `root:<path>` / `repo:<name>` hints; `issue-flow agent resolve [--json]`; the one workspace repo on a `^\d+-` branch; the one `.issueflows/` scaffold in view; the `issueflow-workspace.toml` default (say you used it). Still ambiguous → **stop and ask**. Then use `git -C <project_root>` (or `issue-flow agent … -C <project_root>`) and pass `--repo <owner/repo>` to every `gh` call (`gh repo view` takes the repo positionally).
